<title>SRI LANKA: CRICKET-BANGLADESH, INDIA ASIA CUP MATCH DELAYED.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-BANGLADESH, INDIA ASIA CUP MATCH DELAYED.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Asia Cup match between Bangladesh and India was delayed on Thursday because of heavy overnight rain at Colombo's Singahalese Sports Club ground, officials said.</p>
<p>The match, originally due to start at 10.30 a.m. (0430 GMT), had been postponed until around noon, they said.</p>
<p>India need to restrict Bangladesh to a total of less than 150 runs and then knock the runs off in 20 overs if they are to reach the final against Sri Lanka on Saturday.</p>
</text>
